    "body": "> Testing locally with both your provided starship configs on fish and iTerm, I am unable to reproduce the bug you're encountering.\r\n> \r\n> I see that you have a bit of shell configuration showing `(base)` on the right, which may be affecting the prompt from working correctly.\r\n> \r\n> Could you please share your full shell config (`~/.config/fish/config.fish`) and Starship config that reproduces the issue?\r\n\r\nHi! yes of course.\r\n\r\nThe fish config at that path is:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n\r\n# >>> conda initialize >>>\r\n# !! Contents within this block are managed by 'conda init' !!\r\neval /Users/jaimeferrando/miniconda3/bin/conda \"shell.fish\" \"hook\" $argv | source\r\n# <<< conda initialize <<<\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe starship config is the one on the first post, posting it here again:\r\n\r\n```\r\n# ~/.dotfiles/startship/starship.toml\r\n\r\n# makes prompt a single line\r\nadd_newline = false\r\n\r\n[line_break]\r\ndisabled = true\r\n\r\n[python]\r\ndisabled = true\r\n\r\n[git_branch]\r\nformat = \"on[$symbol$branch]($style) \"\r\nstyle = \"bold yellow\"\r\nsymbol = \"🍣 \"\r\n```",
