    "body": "@matchai  I have a similar issue and tried replicating it with the config provided by @jiwidi, however it didn't happen. It did however happen with a different emoji:\r\n\r\n#### Environment\r\n- Starship version: 0.54.0\r\n- fish version: fish, version 3.2.2\r\n- Operating system: Mac OS 10.14.5\r\n- Terminal emulator: iTerm.app 3.4.7beta2\r\n- Git Commit Hash: \r\n- Branch/Tag: \r\n- Rust Version: rustc 1.51.0\r\n- Rust channel:  release\r\n- Build Time: 2021-05-15 15:29:31\r\n#### Relevant Shell Configuration\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nstarship init fish | source\r\n```\r\n\r\n#### Starship Configuration\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n# ~/.dotfiles/startship/starship.toml\r\n\r\n# makes prompt a single line\r\nadd_newline = false\r\n\r\n[line_break]\r\ndisabled = true\r\n\r\n[python]\r\ndisabled = true\r\n\r\n[git_branch]\r\n# format = \"[$symbol$branch]($style) \"\r\nformat = \"[$symbol]($style) \"\r\nstyle = \"bold yellow\"\r\nsymbol = \"☁️ \"\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nAbove is output generated by `starship bug-report`\r\n\r\nedit: Btw, if I try to record the issue using `asciicinema`, everything displays perfectly in the video that's produced. I'm not sure how their tech works under the hood, but I thought I would share in case it's a clue to the issue.",
